                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>How is the Saudi Arabia jewelry market different from Dubai?</h3>
                                        <p>2nd-largest GCC market + fastest-growing due to Vision 2030 + female-buyer autonomy shifts. Snapchat-dominant platform mix (vs Instagram-Meta in Dubai). Arabic-first creative essential (vs trilingual acceptable in Dubai). Halal + culturally-conservative messaging non-negotiable (stricter than Dubai). SASO compliance + 15% VAT (vs UAE 5%).</p>
                                        <h3>Why is Snapchat so important in KSA jewelry marketing?</h3>
                                        <p>KSA has the world's highest Snapchat penetration per capita. Arabic-speaker + young Saudi female demographic heavily on Snapchat. Snapchat carries 40-60% of KSA jewelry paid + organic reach. Snapchat ads + Snapchat AR + Snapchat Discover essential. Agencies without Snapchat capability cannot serve KSA jewelry brands effectively.</p>
                                        <h3>What creative sensitivities must KSA jewelry marketing respect?</h3>
                                        <p>Halal-compliant (no alcohol, no pork, no non-Islamic imagery), culturally-conservative model + imagery (modest dress, head-covering), family + gifting + heritage narratives (rather than individual + self-expression), modesty + luxury framing (elegant rather than ostentatious). Non-compliance triggers ad rejection + brand damage.</p>
                                        <h3>When are the peak jewelry-buying periods in Saudi Arabia?</h3>
                                        <p>Ramadan + Eid al-Fitr + Eid al-Adha (moving lunar calendar), Umrah + Hajj tourism seasons, wedding season year-round, Saudi National Day (Sept 23), founding day (Feb 22). Calendar-plan 6-8 weeks pre-peak with Arabic-first culturally-appropriate creative.</p>
                                        <h3>What compliance must KSA jewelry brands handle?</h3>
                                        <p>SASO (Saudi Standardization) hallmarking + purity (equivalent to India BIS), Kimberley Process for diamonds, KSA 15% VAT registration + invoicing, cross-border shipping + duty for imports + exports, halal certification for jewelry components where applicable.</p>
                                        <h3>What is Vision 2030 and how does it affect jewelry marketing?</h3>
                                        <p>Saudi Vision 2030 is the KSA transformation plan driving female-workforce participation + tourism (Umrah + Hajj scaling) + entertainment + retail liberalisation + digital-commerce acceleration. Effect on jewelry marketing: female-buyer autonomy shifts (women buying jewelry directly rather than family purchase), digital-first D2C acceleration, tourism-driven purchase behavior, and new brand + creative opportunities in previously-restricted contexts.</p>
                                        <h3>What is a realistic agency retainer for a KSA jewelry brand?</h3>
                                        <p>Rs 2-5 lakh / month (SAR 8,500-21,500) for Starter-to-Growth. Rs 5-12 lakh / month (SAR 21,500-52,000) for Enterprise + luxury. KSA-specific Snapchat + Arabic-native creative capability may add 10-20% premium. Ad spend separate + typically SAR 25,000-250,000 / month depending on tier.</p>
                                        <h3>Does ITD have KSA jewelry work?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes. Published city-specific jewelry marketing playbooks for Jeddah + Dammam + Al Khobar + Doha under our GCC jewelry vertical work. Additional Riyadh work + client references available under NDA on discovery call. See <a href="/services/gcc/jeddah-jewellery-agency.php">Jeddah jewellery agency page</a> + Dammam + Al Khobar pages for KSA-specific playbooks.</p>
